      "problem": "Given that $f(x)={x}^{2}$, the instantaneous rate of change ${f}^{′}(-1)$ can be computed using the limit of a difference quotient. The first few steps of this calculation are shown below:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-1) & ={lim}_{h\\to 0}\\frac{f(-1+h)-f(-1)}{h} \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to 0}\\frac{(-1+h)^{2}-(-1)^{2}}{h} \\\\  & =…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinish the calculation, and hence find ${f}^{′}(-1).$",
